==French==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|fr}} {{m|frm|laisser}}, from {{etyl|fro|fr}} {{m|fro|lesser}}, {{m|fro|lessier}}, {{m|fro|laissier||to let, let go, leave}}, from {{etyl|la|fr}} {{m|la|laxō|laxō, laxāre|to relax, loosen}}; partly from or influenced by {{etyl|goh|fr}} {{m|goh|lāzzan}}, {{m|goh|lāzan||to let, let go, leave}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|lassen}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{m|gem-pro|*lētaną||to let, leave, leave alone}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|fr}} {{m|ine-pro|*lēy-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*lēi-d-||to leave, let}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|sc=Latinx|lǣtan||to allow, let go, leave, rent}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌻𐌴𐍄𐌰𐌽||to release, forgive}}. Conflated also with {{etyl|fro|-}} {{m|fro|laiier||to leave, abandon, allow}} (compare {{etyl|pro|-}} {{m|pro|laihar}}, {{m|pro|laiar}}, Old Northern {{etyl|it|-}} {{m|it|lagare}}), also of {{etyl|gem|-}} origin, from {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌻𐌰𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽||to lay, let lie, leave}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fr}} {{m|gem-pro|*lagjaną||to lay}}. More at {{l|en|let}}, {{l|en|lay}}.

