==Middle French==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|frm|laissier}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|frm}} {{m|fro|lesser}}, {{m|fro|lessier}}, {{m|fro|laissier||to let, let go, leave}}, from {{etyl|la|frm}} {{m|la|laxō|laxō, laxāre|to relax, loosen}}; partly from or influenced by {{etyl|goh|frm}} {{m|goh|lāzzan}}, {{m|goh|lāzan||to let, let go, leave}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|lassen}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|frm}} {{m|gem-pro|*lētaną||to let, leave, leave alone}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|frm}} {{m|ine-pro|*lēy-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*lēi-d-||to leave, let}}.

===Verb===
{{head|frm|verb}}

# to [[allow]]; to [[permit]]
# to [[leave]] {{gloss|not take}}
# to [[leave alone]] {{gloss|not interfere}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1488|author=Jean Dupré|title=Lancelot du Lac|passage={{lang|frm|[ie] vous prie que vous me '''laissiez''' ceste bataille}}|page=[http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k111060r/f74.item.zoom 74]|translation=I beg of you to let me go into this battle alone}}

